WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- My heart went out to the people that

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.070
produced this stuff in
all of our bad times,

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.730
but especially fine
orchestras and then dancers,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.792
people that do that and you,

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:10.625
- Thank you.

00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:12.450
- I just amazed at what you people do

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.410
and how you express it.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.746
It's art and love and design and movement.

00:00:15.746 --> 00:00:16.579
(crowd cheering)

00:00:16.579 --> 00:00:17.443
- It's beautiful to see
your body flowing like that.

00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:19.560
And that's so cool that y'all get to do

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.393
the father, daughter.

00:00:20.393 --> 00:00:21.510
I thought that was really special.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.343
- What book?

00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:23.790
Tell them, remember that book you read?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.653
- Yeah, it was literally
called Misty Copeland.

00:00:25.653 --> 00:00:26.486
- Ah my god.

00:00:26.486 --> 00:00:27.810
- I had a book that I read when I was like

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.670
- Just saw her backstage
and the look on her face.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.503
- She's like.

00:00:30.503 --> 00:00:31.383
- I was like.

00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:32.216
Who, who?

00:00:32.216 --> 00:00:33.250
- Oh my gosh, that's so funny.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.341
We didn't know that. That's so.

00:00:34.341 --> 00:00:36.570
- Every morning like I would, I was,

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.790
I don't know probably like
seven or eight years old

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.580
and my mom and I, we used
to read books to like

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.140
while she was making breakfast.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.000
And I had, it was just like,
you know, picture books

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.930
like a kid's picture book.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.400
But I read it every morning.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.363
- Oh my God.

00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:49.196
- Like every morning.

00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:50.029
- I love that.

00:00:50.029 --> 00:00:51.540
- So when I heard, I was like.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.373
Who?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.510
- Sitting right next to her.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.597
Just take it in.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:56.514
Take it in.

